     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about double the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual per-dose maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nCould you check what was intended? A few possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose**, if a different strength was meant.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
